wy misty thing you  think the sword is actually gonna do the  soul-sucking thing that does in the  comics that'd be very cool i like the  vibe i like the feel the whole trail is  just very punchy which just feels good  and feels right that said there are a  number of things at particularly in  regards to harley quinn that are making  me nervous now it's not the casting it's  not even really the performance that i  got i have a feeling margot robbie is  probably gonna play this about as well  as it's gonna be played i'm nervous  about the way Harley's being written  though because the lines that she has  and she kind  gets highlighted certainly for longer  periods than almost anybody else and her  lines just they smack of trying too hard  if somebody really going what's the  kookiest thing i can think that could be  said and it just I it's such a fine  balance to write a character like that I  I think to a certain extent when you're  writing you have to dial it back and  just trust that the performers gonna  bring that level of kookiness and  nuttiness to it which is usually what  would happen in the animation her actual  lines were not really one liners are  particularly memorable in and of  themselves but it was the way that way  they were delivered and said that always  made them great it feels like here  they're trying they actually tried to  write lines that were crazy and kooky  but it just comes across as just trying  too hard I can't think of any other  phrase other than that you know I look  at the her voice and the voices in her  head line or the line she has after she  breaks the glass and takes the person  which is a cool action I think that  that's an action that really suits  Harley but then for line after that I'm  like is that mm-hmm and even though  where I'm seeing that is kind of  restricted to Harley in this trailer  itself it makes me nervous for the movie  as a whole because the trying too hard  thing was sort of one of my initial  criticisms when we first saw the first  images of the Joker it looked like they  were trying too hard to make him crazy  and I kind of dial back on that like I  said I I'm kind of digging what I see  about the junker here but now I'm  getting that same vibe off of Harley and  I'm starting to worry that the whole  movie isn't just going to be fun it's  just gonna be trying too hard to be  weird and quirky and I I don't know I  I'm hoping I'm wrong I really do because  there's enough energy and fun in this  trailer that it just makes me excited  way more excited than I am for Batman V  Superman certainly and a million times  more excited than I am about that first  footage of wonder woman that came out I  don't even think I have the energy to do  a video on that but in any case trailer  for The Suicide Squad have you seen it  what did you think about it whatever you  thought drop something down in the  comments and let's talk about it please  go ahead like subscribe check me out on  Twitter at council of geeks check out  the council geeks podcasts on iTunes and  stitcher  and until next time this council is  adjourned
 

